{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jc2gVPQvJBCYAGbyer","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Two of the facts as they stand would make a careful reviewer stop, and your answers decide how I frame them.\n\n1. **Will you still have three attorneys after June?** If the attorney who's leaving isn't replaced with other money, this grant keeps you at two lawyers. That's a very different request from adding a third. Are you funding the replacement separately, or is this grant really paying for the replacement?\n\n2. **Where does the rest of the salary come from?** The attorney costs $156,000 over two years and you're asking for $90,000, which leaves $66,000 uncovered. Reviewers will look for where that comes from. Is it the county contract, another funder, or something else, and is it committed or still pending? What's the outlook for the county renewal in October?\n\n3. **How many more tenants would a third attorney serve?** Your numbers suggest each attorney handles about 80 cases a year. That would make it roughly 80 more tenants a year, about a quarter of the 300 you turned away. Does that match what you'd expect, or do you have a better figure?\n\n4. **What are the names?** I need the clinic, the county and the state, and the foundation's name if it differs from \"[State] Bar Foundation.\"\n\n5. **Does the foundation list priorities or scoring criteria for this round?** Examples would be access to justice in underserved areas, measurable outcomes, or sustainability after the grant ends. If you can paste the summary instructions or criteria, I'll write to them.\n\nIf you don't know an answer, just say so and I'll write around it without guessing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":9572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephem