{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JdGNJF64syaL443Qao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it to stay accurate whatever happens in June, but the departing attorney is something you'll need to address before you submit. Notes are below the draft.\n\n<final_document>\n**Tenant Defense Project: Eviction Defense Staff Attorney**\n\nThe Tenant Defense Project requests $90,000 over two years ($45,000 per year) to fund an additional staff attorney who will represent tenants facing eviction in [County].\n\n**The need.** Last year, 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. Our two attorneys represented the tenant in 163 of them, about one case in seven. We turned away roughly 300 more tenants who asked for help because no attorney was free to take their case. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases. We cannot take on more tenants without adding staff.\n\n**What representation achieves.** Last year, 58% of the cases where we represented the tenant ended with the tenant either staying in the home or getting at least 60 days to move. That time lets a family find new housing and plan the move.\n\n**The project.** The new attorney will carry a full caseload of about 80 tenants a year, drawn from the tenants we now have to turn away. Over the two-year grant, that means about 160 more households will have a lawyer in eviction court. For every case, we will record whether the tenant stayed in the home, got at least 60 days to move, or had another result. We will report these outcomes to [Foundation] each year.\n\n**Budget and match.** The position costs $78,000 a year with benefits, or $156,000 over two years. The grant would pay $90,000 of that. A family fund has pledged $20,000 a year ($40,000 total), and the Tenant Defense Project will pay the remaining $13,000 a year ($26,000 total) from its operating budget. Together these sources fully fund the position for both years.\n</final_document>\n\nThe summary is about 280 words.\n\n1. **The attorney leaving in June.** I called the position \"an additional staff attorney\" rather than \"a third attorney\" and never claimed you'll have three lawyers. If her position isn't refilled, you'd still have two, and the \"160 more households\" figure wouldn't hold. The full application will almost certainly ask about current staffing. Reviewers who learn about the departure later may feel misled, so it's worth deciding how you'll answer that before you submit.\n\n2. **The county contract.** I didn't mention it. Your $13,000-a-year share comes from the operating budget, and that budget depends partly on the $60,000 county contract. If the application asks about sustainability or risks, say plainly that the contract renews in October and describe your plan if it doesn't.\n\n3. **The 58% figure.** I presented it only as your clients' results. I didn't compare it to tenants without a lawyer, since you don't have that number. If you can find a published local or statewide figure for unrepresented tenants, adding it would strengthen this section a lot."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":9974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f105ae72-0adc-4d6f-aeb9-6961087ed681","uuid":"274b70d5-46a5-4816-8f91-05ddf4b1ece4","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:19:27.276Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7JdG6vGPMiHXBdwpQbX"}
